<title>USA: Spec's Music Q3 loss widens.</title>
<headline>Spec's Music Q3 loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>MIAMI 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Third Quarter</p>
<p>						   Ended April 30,</p>
<p>						   1997		 1996</p>
<p> Revenues			     $ 16,510,000     $ 17,929,000</p>
<p> Loss before income taxes	  (1,380,000)	(1,308,000)</p>
<p>Provision (benefit) for</p>
<p>    income taxes			   678,000	  (496,000)</p>
<p> Net loss				(2,058,000)	  (812,000)</p>
<p> Net loss per share			  (.39)		(.15)</p>
<p> Shares outstanding		    5,254,000	  5,449,000</p>
<p>						   Nine Months</p>
<p>						   Ended April 30,</p>
<p>						   1997		 1996</p>
<p> Revenues			     $ 53,760,000     $ 60,881,000</p>
<p> Loss before income taxe	   (3,277,000)	(2,246,000)</p>
<p>Provision (benefit) for</p>
<p>    income taxes			  (28,000)	  (853,000)</p>
<p> Net loss				(3,249,000)	(1,393,000)</p>
<p> Net loss per share			  (.62)		(.25)</p>
<p> Shares outstanding		    5,249,000	  5,492,000</p>
<p>NOTES: Full Company name is Spec's Music Inc.</p>
<p>The company said revenues fell because it is operating fewer stores than a year ago. Same store sales rose 3.1 percent.</p>
<p>Q4 earnings were affected by a charge on deferred asset amounts for future carrybacks of operating losses.</p>
</text>
